Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.00,0:00:41.00,Default,,0,0,0,,0 · Publisher / CTV\NA mid-roll is about to fire. This is the OpenRTB the exchange is holding. ARTF lets an agent rewrite it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.20,0:01:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,1 · SSP · looks legal, is not\NWrong lifecycle, wrong ids, missing paths. One legacy write would have landed. We still drop the set.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.20,0:01:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,2 · Engineer · mutation fine, auction not\NADD_METRICS value "high". Well-formed ARTF. After apply, OpenRTB is not.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.20,0:02:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,3 · DSP · curation lands\NNew segments, new deal, floor $12 to $14.50, viewability 0.82. The DSP bids on the rewritten ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.20,0:03:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,4 · Publisher · a deal leaves the wire\NSUPPRESS_DEALS pulls deal-standard. Curation is allowed to do that. The path still has to be this auction.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.20,0:03:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,5 · DSP · the bid is shaded\NResponse-stage hop. $18.40 in, $12.88 out. Same dummy, new clearing price.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.20,0:04:13.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Volume · same hop, many living rooms\NSynthetic mix at 200/s. 90% clean, 8% illegal, 2% breaking. Real gRPC. Not an exchange's QPS.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.20,0:04:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Grafana · real rtblint-grpc\Np99 against a 150ms tmax. Drops are the dirty mix. Shed should sit at zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.20,0:05:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The bid hop\NEnvelope, mutation, applied. VASTlint was the creative hop. This is the bid hop. Independent. Not an IAB product.
